-- 0353 (13/9/2026): drop stray internal ASCII spaces from barcode identity.
-- Owner report: 125 catalog items stored as "1  XXXX" (bytes 20 20) — Excel/manual-entry noise the
-- browser collapses to one visible space; no scanner/typist reproduces it, so those items were
-- unscannable/unsearchable/unsellable. (1) Clean raw values so display/scan/type agree; (2) regenerate
-- barcodeNormalized so it also drops internal 0x20 (lockstep with canonicalizeBarcodeInput).
-- Verified on production: the 125 spaced rows strip to 0 collisions (all distinct, pattern 1XXXX).
-- UPDATE IGNORE (defense-in-depth): raw `barcode` is UNIQUE; if some other environment (or a row added
-- between verification and deploy) held a spaced barcode that strips onto an existing value, a plain
-- UPDATE would raise ER_DUP_ENTRY and abort the deploy. IGNORE skips only such a colliding row, leaving
-- it raw — it stays matchable because the regenerated barcodeNormalized (indexed, NOT unique) still
-- strips it, and two codes that collapse to one identity correctly resolve as AMBIGUOUS, never a
-- silent wrong-owner pick (§5). On production all 125 are cleaned (0 collisions).
UPDATE IGNORE `productUnits` SET `barcode` = REPLACE(`barcode`, ' ', '') WHERE `barcode` LIKE '% %';
